      "observed": "REG2.1 is on +3.3V, while +3V3 is a separate net. All listed VDD pins on both MCUs are unconnected rather than on either rail.",
      "expected": "The specification says the 3.3 V rail feeds both MCUs. Their VDD pins should be connected to the regulator output rail.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"+3.3V\") ... (node (ref \"REG2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"OUT\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"2\") (name \"+3V3\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"217\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"277\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC1-VDD-Pad19)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3.3V feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU has its required VDD supply in the represented connectivity, so the flight computers cannot operate; the regulator output is also isolated from the separate +3V3 net.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["HSE1", "HSE2", "FCC1", "NAVC1"],
      "pins": ["HSE1.1", "HSE1.3", "HSE2.1", "HSE2.3", "FCC1.5", "FCC1.37", "FCC1.12", "FCC1.13", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC", "Net-(FCC1-PH0)", "VREF+_FCC", "Net-(NAVC1-PH0)", "Net-(NAVC1-PH1)"],
      "observed": "The FCC crystal nets connect to FCC1 pins 5 (PE6) and 37 (PE7), not its PH0/PH1 oscillator pins. The NAVC crystal nets do not connect to NAVC1 at all; its PH0 and PH1 pins are on separate nets.",
      "expected": "The specification identifies a 25 MHz HSE crystal for each MCU; each crystal should connect to that MCU's HSE input and output pins (FCC1.12/.13 and NAVC1.5/.6 per the supplied pin definitions).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"31\") (name \"HSE_IN_FCC\") ... (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PE6\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"33\") (name \"HSE_OUT_FCC\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"37\") (pinfunction \"PE7\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"32\") (name \"HSE_IN_NAVC\") ... (node (ref \"HSE2\") (pin \"1\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"90\") (name \"Net-(NAVC1-PH0)\") ... (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"5\") (pinfunction \"PH0\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The external 25 MHz clocks are not correctly provided to either MCU. The FCC crystal is wired to GPIOs, and the NAVC crystal is disconnected from its oscillator pins, potentially preventing intended clock operation or forcing fallback clocking.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["FCC1", "UART3_FCC1"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.48", "FCC1.73", "UART3_FCC1.3", "UART3_FCC1.4"],
      "nets": ["UART3_TX_FCC", "UART3_RX_FCC"],
      "observed": "The nets labeled UART3_TX_FCC and UART3_RX_FCC connect to FCC1 pins 48 and 73, both identified as VCAP, and are also routed to the UART3 connector.",
      "expected": "UART3 connector signals should connect to MCU UART transmit/receive GPIOs; VCAP pins should not be used as UART signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"145\") (name \"UART3_RX_FCC\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"73\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"147\") (name \"UART3_TX_FCC\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(pin (num \"48\") (name \"VCAP\") (type \"power_out\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The UART3 connector cannot provide the labeled serial interface and instead exposes the MCU's VCAP supply pins, which can disrupt the MCU's internal regulator and risk damage if externally driven.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomalies are present: both MCUs' VDD pins are unconnected, the 3.3 V nets are split, and neither MCU's 25 MHz crystal is correctly connected. The FCC UART3 connector is also wired to VCAP pins rather than UART-capable GPIOs."
}

